{"id": "EUVD-2026-26559", "enisaUuid": "f09847cd-c180-3b73-9360-8ecff13f48b8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/zcrypt: Fix memory leak with CCA cards used as accelerator\n\nTests showed that there is a memory leak if CCA cards are used as\naccelerator for clear key RSA requests (ME and CRT). With the last\nrework for the memory allocation the AP messages are allocated by\nap_init_apmsg() but for some reason on two places (ME and CRT) the\nolder allocation was still in place. So the first allocation simple\nwas never freed.", "datePublished": "2026-05-01T14:14:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:39:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1650268579e1113b30402dbcca4dba6589a0fccf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/586222c37d4027dbf60a604fbe820184fee7c1c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ace37bfec3822033e59fff390f2ff99fc96ebe4f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c8d46f17c2fc7d25c18e60c008928aecab26184d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-31746", "GHSA-rvh3-5jfr-6p58"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3d51701b-9670-35de-93cc-65090f7c9ed0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19.12"}, {"id": "4763caff-1571-3ac4-b653-c85b6edee680", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "4d9cc83c-50c7-3eeb-be7c-e8f05cc1ea6b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "57db62a130ce69e6f3a870cf1119d8f860391f97 <ace37bfec3822033e59fff390f2ff99fc96ebe4f"}, {"id": "60368e1f-e6dd-39b6-bb6d-e69aa53eefea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "57db62a130ce69e6f3a870cf1119d8f860391f97 <c8d46f17c2fc7d25c18e60c008928aecab26184d"}, {"id": "806be938-a667-37b2-af24-c03300989172", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.16"}, {"id": "8cb72082-2fa4-3b9e-b16f-f4a4e1d8656d"